agents are evaluated in RecreationWorld, a five-platform framework that provides reproducible environments with      
native GUI control and coding tools, using running references as oracles for hidden behavioral tests [^2609.22000].  
In health interventions, an agentic Just-in-Time Adaptive Intervention (JITAI) system autonomously reviews personal  
sleep and behavioral data to adapt reminders and interventions, demonstrating technical feasibility for personalized 
health support [^2609.21805].                                                                                        

Multi-Agent Control, Robotics, and Strategic Games                                                                   

Coordinated multi-agent systems continue to push boundaries in physical and strategic domains. Multi-Agent           
Event-Triggered LQG Control addresses shared communication constraints by decoupling optimal control laws across     
agents while formulating a globally coupled transmission schedule as a mixed-integer linear program, optimized via a 
receding-horizon scheduler [^2609.21974]. In robotics, MAAP enables collaborative manipulation by treating every     
robotic arm as a dual-purpose active perception device, predicting role-dependent actions within a single network to 
significantly boost success rates in multi-wrist scenarios [^2609.21929]. VIRGA coordinates heterogeneous air-ground 
platforms by converting dual-LiDAR observations into bounded Riemannian fields mediated by a virtual agent with      
reciprocal elastic feedback, ensuring safe navigation in confined geometries [^2609.21883]. Theoretical multi-agent  
decision-making is advanced through the Matrix Exponential Fixed-Point Iteration with Annealing (MEFPIA) algorithm,  
which efficiently searches for equilibrium points in extended Gutoski-Watrous quantum games by avoiding explicit     
construction of full joint density matrices [^2609.21944].                                                           

Agent Governance, Trust, and Safety                                                                                  

Security and authorization boundaries are rigorously tested by APort Vault, which replays thousands of human-written 
attacks against live payment agents to evaluate policy configurations and the Open Agent Passport specification,     
demonstrating near-zero unauthorized transfers behind the authorization layer [^2609.22076]. Containment strategies  
are formalized through Provisional Reachability, which holds every agent crossing in escrow for auditing and         
revocation, mathematically bounding information leakage and preventing secret assembly across windows [^2609.21957]. 
Policy-regulated multi-agent systems are structured by the JustAct framework, providing a Rocq specification and Rust
implementation for open-multi-agent environments with enforceable policy constraints [^10.5281_zenodo.21240014].     
Enterprise governance is further refined by the Agent Steward concept, which identifies context provenance and       
temporal validity as a missing architectural dimension to detect silent errors caused by obsolete agent context,     
introducing the Context Validity Declaration to make obsolescence detectable at runtime [^10.5281_zenodo.21660204].  

Societal, Enterprise, and Specialized Applications                                                                   

The integration of agents into enterprise and specialized workflows demands rigorous evaluation and value alignment. 
EnterpriseVal introduces a use-case-level evaluation system that maps metric vectors with confidence bounds to       
REJECT/CONDITIONAL/SCALE decisions, closing the gap between public benchmarks and deployment readiness [^2609.21841].
In industrial settings, LLM-based systems for root cause analysis of test failures are compared in single-agent      
versus orchestrated multi-agent configurations, revealing that single-agent setups currently offer faster, lower-cost
