+                                                                               
+## Agent Memory and Reasoning Mechanisms                                       
+Recent research has significantly advanced how agents manage, retrieve, and    
reason over information. Designer-RSI introduces a continual adaptation         
framework where a frozen frontier model accumulates and refines reusable        
procedural memories from user traffic, widening its skill bank through          
successful and failed executions without weight updates [^2609.22086]. To       
improve the reliability of memory retrieval, the Memory Decision Layer (MDL)    
proposes a zero-parameter controller that fuses relevance, reliability, and task
risk to explicitly decouple confidence from consistency, drastically reducing   
hallucination rates under conflicting memories [^2609.22043]. Long-term         
conversational memory is further addressed by AutoViewMem, which organizes      
memories into self-configuring, low-overlap semantic views to prevent semantic  
interference and improve top-K retrieval accuracy [^2609.21940]. In interactive 
settings, RAVEL employs retrieval-aware online reinforcement learning to        
optimize question generation policies, dynamically reallocating questioning     
budgets toward attributes that yield the most useful retrieval evidence         
[^2609.21924]. Furthermore, opinion dynamics in social simulations are made     
auditable and controllable through Bayesian Chronicle Agents, which separate    
belief states from linguistic output and update stances via single Bayesian     
steps per utterance [^2609.21997].                                              
+                                                                               
+## Agent Environments and Training Paradigms                                   
+The development of robust agents relies heavily on scalable environments and   
targeted training methodologies. MintAct unifies UI grounding, multi-step       
navigation, and visual tool use across mobile, desktop, and web platforms,      
leveraging a scalable reinforcement learning infrastructure that maintains      
stability under noisy feedback and off-policy drift [^2609.22083]. For software 
development, CodeMidas scales agentic coding environments by transforming       
implemented functionality in open-source codebases into executable RL tasks,    
improving performance across issue repair, whole-program construction, and      
terminal work benchmarks [^2609.22068]. Hybrid computer-use agents are evaluated
in RecreationWorld, a five-platform framework that provides reproducible        
environments with native GUI control and coding tools, using running references 
as oracles for hidden behavioral tests [^2609.22000]. In health interventions,  
an agentic Just-in-Time Adaptive Intervention (JITAI) system autonomously       
reviews personal sleep and behavioral data to adapt reminders and interventions,
demonstrating technical feasibility for personalized health support             
[^2609.21805].                                                                  
+                                                                               
+## Multi-Agent Control, Robotics, and Strategic Games                          
+Coordinated multi-agent systems continue to push boundaries in physical and    
strategic domains. Multi-Agent Event-Triggered LQG Control addresses shared     
communication constraints by decoupling optimal control laws across agents while
formulating a globally coupled transmission schedule as a mixed-integer linear  
program, optimized via a receding-horizon scheduler [^2609.21974]. In robotics, 
MAAP enables collaborative manipulation by treating every robotic arm as a      
dual-purpose active perception device, predicting role-dependent actions within 
a single network to significantly boost success rates in multi-wrist scenarios  
[^2609.21929]. VIRGA coordinates heterogeneous air-ground platforms by          
converting dual-LiDAR observations into bounded Riemannian fields mediated by a 
virtual agent with reciprocal elastic feedback, ensuring safe navigation in     
confined geometries [^2609.21883]. Theoretical multi-agent decision-making is   
advanced through the Matrix Exponential Fixed-Point Iteration with Annealing    
(MEFPIA) algorithm, which efficiently searches for equilibrium points in        
extended Gutoski-Watrous quantum games by avoiding explicit construction of full
joint density matrices [^2609.21944].                                           
                                                                                

